# AGI in Healthcare

## Overview
This project explores how Artificial General Intelligence (AGI) could transform the healthcare industry. Unlike traditional AI, AGI can adapt and apply knowledge across multiple tasks, making it more effective for complex medical decision-making.

## Key Areas
- Personalized medicine using patient data  
- AI-assisted diagnosis and treatment planning  
- Hospital operations and resource optimization  
- Real-time health monitoring systems  

## What I Learned
- The difference between narrow AI and AGI  
- How data impacts healthcare decisions  
- The role of AI in improving efficiency and accuracy  

## Challenges
- Patient data privacy concerns  
- Bias in medical datasets  
- Ethical responsibility in AI-driven decisions  

